WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.668
 Todd, Michael,
congratulations.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.070
You've made it into the final
round of this competition,

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.939
which means that you're
both one step closer

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:08.807
to the title of Forged
in Fire champion

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:10.977
and that check for $10,000.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.812
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.781
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:19.786
That weapon is the Kampilan.

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:23.289
Good luck.

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:24.624
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:33.032
MICHAEL: Feels really good to be
home and back in my home forge.

00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:35.334
The Kampilan is
completely new to me.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.436
Part of this is a
historical recreation,

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:41.140
so it's really important I
make it historically accurate.

00:00:41.206 --> 00:00:43.243
All right, here's my new sword.

00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:48.414
That's good.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.184
I'm really nervous, because
it doesn't take much for this

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.652
to get messed up.

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:57.022
I feel I can do it, but I
just have to stay on task.

00:00:57.122 --> 00:00:59.859
Looks pretty good.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.127
My goal today was to
have a profiled sword.

00:01:02.227 --> 00:01:04.063
That happened, and now
I'm a little further

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.365
ahead than I anticipated.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:06.199
I'm beat.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.270
TODD: Yesterday, I had
the up side of the motor

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:16.008
on the power hammer and
forged out my piece.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:17.243
There you go.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.612
That looks like the picture.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.849
Today, I want to make sure I
get that thing all tapered,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:23.982
narrowed down.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.451
Getting the weight
off the blade,

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:29.289
and trying to thin that
down as a task in itself.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.924
I hope I have it
thin enough for Doug.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.125
Hopefully, it'll satisfy him.

00:01:33.225 --> 00:01:35.194
It's getting a lot lighter.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:38.164
Ready for heat treatment.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.132
Quenching is a real
critical thing.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:41.767
You don't want to
hear that little tink,

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.203
you know, that crack sound.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:50.676
Oh.

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:52.178
[chuckling]

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.914
No cracks, no warps.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:59.018
[inaudible] Yes, I'm
very happy with it.

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.186
Lord, thank you.

00:02:03.188 --> 00:02:04.790
MICHAEL: Today I'm
going to cut spur

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:06.325
out of the tip of the blade.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.694
All right, here we go.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.429
There's a lot of bad things
that can happen here.

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:13.065
Taking a chisel to
any part of your blade

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:16.536
can result in
unfixable blemishes.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.341
I'll take it.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.776
Time for the heat treat.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:29.015
Heat treat's the worst part
of any blade making process,

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:31.985
so I'm incredibly nervous.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:35.387
Warping is the number
one concern I have.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.289
When I dunk the
blade into that oil,

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:38.490
it's going to do what
it's going to do,

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.360
and there's nothing
I can do to stop it.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.703
My gut wrenches.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:51.737
Warp.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:53.239
That sucks.

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:55.541
The thinner the
steel, the more tricky

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:59.145
it can be to get the heat treat
to go off without any issues.

00:02:59.211 --> 00:03:01.414
But as I look at it, I like it.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.583
Took kind of a scimitar
warp, adds character.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.619
It doesn't go side to side, it
bows up, kind of like a katana.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.256
That is the best word
you can possibly take on.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.358 line:14%
I will take it.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.960 line:8%
 Today I think the plan
is probably eating sawdust.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.396 line:8%
I'm going to work
on that handle.

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:20.266
The way it's designed
is a little unusual.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:24.537
The handle has protruding Y
that comes up towards your arm.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:27.340
It looks like it would be
uncomfortable to yield,

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.941
but it's their blade.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.443
I'm just making it.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.579
Mark up the front guard,
and cut that one out.

00:03:33.645 --> 00:03:36.215
I'm going to do the
top guard as one piece

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:38.150
and fit it to the handle.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:41.153
Does kind of look
like a raptor, kinda.

00:03:41.253 --> 00:03:42.855
It's not what I was
going for, but that's

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:43.923
what it turned out to be.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.191
It's a dinosword.

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:46.325
[laughing]

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.394
I'm a little
apprehensive on testing.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.129
If something
crucially goes wrong,

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:51.564
I won't have a blade to turn in.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:55.468
So I'm going to leave this
to the judges to test.

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:56.202
Very nice.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.704
It looks good.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.605
It's a done deal.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:02.375
 This is my last day.

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.742
I feel pretty good.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.445
Just need grind the tank,
finish off the handle

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.379
and just make stuff
pretty and sharp.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.215
The handle material was
a big block of mahogany.

00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:10.850
Mahogany is a traditional wood.

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:14.153
It's tough, it's rot resistant,
so I don't have too many

00:04:14.253 --> 00:04:15.855
concerns about going into this.

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:20.059
Getting this handle put on and
that is the point of no return.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:22.395
My only reservations with
this blade that it's hefty.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:23.929
A lot of my research
points to the fact

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:25.364
that this is a heavy sword.

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:29.902
For the royal flare of the
sword, genuine human hair.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.171
That is something that
was on these handles,

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:35.041
so it's merely for
historical accuracy.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.074
And it's funny.

00:04:36.141 --> 00:04:36.975
[chuckling]

00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:39.344
Well, it's a Kampilan.

00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:40.546
 All right, gentlemen.

00:04:40.612 --> 00:04:42.315
To test the sharpness
of your blades,

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:45.685
I'll be chopping through our
cat's cradle of rope here.

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:46.585
Todd, you're up first.

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:47.553
You ready?

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:48.354
 I am.

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:55.061
[ropes snapping]

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:06.439
 All right, Todd, this blade
has all the weight right here.

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:09.175
You know it's a weapon that's
designed to be used one

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:11.744
or two handed, but
controlling all

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.146
that forward weight
definitely puts

00:05:14.212 --> 00:05:17.049
this as a two hand only sword.

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:21.120
It's a good looking piece,
and it definitely is a cutter.

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:21.887
Michael, you're up.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:22.888
You ready?

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:23.790
 Let's do it.

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:37.837
[ropes snapping]

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:40.106
 Still a very heavy weapon.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:41.573
I'd have zero
confidence swinging

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:44.476
this one handed that it
wouldn't get away from me.

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:46.946
But the weight
distribution on your blade

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.949
is further back, which
gave me quite a bit more

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:52.851
control to chop those ropes.

00:05:52.951 --> 00:05:57.056
It's definitely a cutter,
so good job, nicely done.

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:58.224
 Thank you

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.626
 Bladesmiths, this
is the kill test.

00:06:00.692 --> 00:06:03.162
I'm going to take your Kampilan
and deliver lethal blows

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:04.630
on this big carcass.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:05.864
Todd, you're up first.
You ready?

00:06:05.931 --> 00:06:06.766
 I sure am.

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:16.042
[blade slashing]

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.117
 All right, Todd.

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:27.887
The swing over here almost cut
all the way, and, of course,

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:32.491
with an easy swing on the way
back, it cut the pig in half.

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:35.193
The Kampilan will kill.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.228
 Thank you.

00:06:36.294 --> 00:06:37.363
 All right, Michael, your turn.

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:38.164
You ready?

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:38.998
 Let's do it.

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:45.638
[blade slashing]

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:54.847
 All right, Mike.

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:56.649
So even though it
is a heavier blade,

00:06:56.715 --> 00:07:00.319
it's counterbalance
allowed to wield going

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:02.721
forward and backward easily.

00:07:02.788 --> 00:07:06.192
So it was an easy recovery
for the final chop.

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:09.795
Overall, your
Kampilan will kill.

00:07:09.862 --> 00:07:10.362
 Thank you.

00:07:10.429 --> 00:07:11.263
HOST: Good job

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.597
 All right, gentlemen.

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:14.600
To test the strength and
durability of your blade,

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:17.570
I'll be chopping into
this green bamboo.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.805
 Bamboo, it's hard stuff.

00:07:19.871 --> 00:07:23.275
If you didn't harden your blade
right, there's a flaw in it,

00:07:23.375 --> 00:07:24.443
this will tell it.

00:07:24.509 --> 00:07:29.815
I am praying that
my edge holds up.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:33.853
[blade chopping]

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:45.531
 Whoa.

00:07:45.597 --> 00:07:49.502
 Yeah, I don't feel any
damage whatsoever on the edge.

00:07:49.568 --> 00:07:52.371
It did a job on that
bamboo and it's clean.

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:53.238
Well done.

00:07:53.338 --> 00:07:54.206
 Thank you.

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:55.541
HOST: Michael, you ready?

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:56.308
 Let's do it.

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:57.143
HOST: OK.

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:06.219
[blade chopping]

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:24.436
Well, I thought I saw
something, but it was just

00:08:24.503 --> 00:08:27.339
bamboo stuck to your blade.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:28.173
It's fine.

00:08:28.273 --> 00:08:29.708
There's no damage there.

00:08:29.808 --> 00:08:33.379
The blade hasn't
changed shape at all.

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:35.748
Good job, well done.

00:08:35.814 --> 00:08:37.416
 All right, bladesmiths,
from the moment you

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:39.818
guys lit those coal
forges until this moment,

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:41.687
you've put in a
lot of hard work.

00:08:41.753 --> 00:08:43.555
There's been a lot of stress.

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:45.157
But in this arena
of competition,

00:08:45.224 --> 00:08:47.560
there can only be one
Forged in Fire champion,

00:08:47.626 --> 00:08:49.595
and that champion is Michael.

00:08:49.662 --> 00:08:53.332
Congratulations, you are
the Forged in Fire champion.

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:56.802
Todd, unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:08:56.902 --> 00:09:00.473
 Todd, this is what we judges
expect in the third round,

00:09:00.539 --> 00:09:02.875
two beautiful blades,
equally matched.

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:05.644
But it comes down to
the finer details.

00:09:05.744 --> 00:09:08.580 line:8%
Your blade isn't
as well balanced

00:09:08.647 --> 00:09:10.783 line:8%
as that of your
opponents, and your design

00:09:10.849 --> 00:09:12.785 line:14%
and detail were not as strong.

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:15.688 line:8%
So for those reasons,
we have to let you go.

00:09:17.956 --> 00:09:21.560
 Be proud of your work Todd,
because it was a close call.

00:09:21.627 --> 00:09:23.995
But please surrender
your weapon.

00:09:24.096 --> 00:09:26.965
TODD: I never thought
about making it this far.

00:09:27.032 --> 00:09:29.668
This is the first
sword I've ever made.

00:09:29.734 --> 00:09:33.105
I'm proud of what I did,
and it held up good.

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:36.608
I didn't think that I would
be capable of doing this.

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:41.180
You never know what kind
of strength you can find.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.515
 Michael, congratulations.

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.049
You are the Forged
in Fire champion,

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:47.586
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:47.652 --> 00:09:49.221
Good job, brother

00:09:49.288 --> 00:09:51.523
[clapping]

00:09:51.623 --> 00:09:53.158
All right what's going
on inside of there?

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:55.460
 It is surreal.

00:09:55.527 --> 00:09:57.463
Wasn't expected,
starting this competition

00:09:57.529 --> 00:09:59.765
but a huge affirmation
of my skills.

00:09:59.831 --> 00:10:03.535
 Please present your
weapon to the judges.

00:10:03.635 --> 00:10:04.603
MICHAEL: It's surreal.

00:10:04.703 --> 00:10:06.472
It hasn't really set in yet.

00:10:06.539 --> 00:10:10.343
All the years that I've put into
this hobby, this craft, and now

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:12.244
to be here and be
the Forged in Fire

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:15.214
champion, it's pretty amazing.

